//@version=6
// For the every-update cadence (05-every-update-lower-bars.json).
//
// `calc_on_every_tick=true` is what Pinelive's config gate requires before it
// will accept `live.cadence: "every-update"`. Be aware of what that flag does
// and does not do:
//
//   - In piner it is INERT METADATA. The realtime driver executes the script on
//     every update it is handed, regardless of this value. The cadence is
//     decided entirely by what Pinelive feeds the engine.
//   - So this flag is a consent gate: you are asserting the script tolerates
//     being re-evaluated several times per bar, with piner rolling its broker
//     state back to the last committed bar before each revision.
//
// A script under every-update must therefore not assume it runs once per bar.
// It also may not use request.security at all — Pinelive rejects every security
// dependency for this cadence.
strategy("Intrabar SMA cross (every-update)",
     overlay = true,
     initial_capital = 10000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value = 50,
     calc_on_every_tick = true,
     process_orders_on_close = true)

fastLength = input.int(10, "fast", minval = 1)
slowLength = input.int(30, "slow", minval = 2)

fast = ta.sma(close, fastLength)
slow = ta.sma(close, slowLength)

if ta.crossover(fast, slow)
    strategy.entry("long", strategy.long)
if ta.crossunder(fast, slow)
    strategy.close("long")

plot(fast, "fast", color = color.teal)
plot(slow, "slow", color = color.orange)
